# INTENTIONALLY EMPTY. NEVER PUT A SECRET IN THIS FILE — it is tracked in git.
#
# Its emptiness IS its function. `wrangler deploy` auto-loads .env.local, which
# on a machine set up for data uploads defines CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN — the
# narrowly-scoped R2 token (see scripts/upload_bundles_r2.mts). That token
# SHADOWS the wrangler OAuth login: an env-var token always wins, so every
# `wrangler deploy` authenticates as the R2 token, which has no
# workers_scripts:write and cannot deploy. The symptom is an auth failure that
# looks like "you are not logged in" while `wrangler login` has in fact been run.
#
# Passing --env-file replaces that automatic discovery, so pointing it at this
# empty file leaves the OAuth credentials in play. Both credentials are needed
# and neither can replace the other: OAuth is not granted R2 scopes, and the R2
# token is not granted Workers scopes.
#
# Used by `pnpm run deploy:cf`.
